 "section_summary": "This section comprises two copies of U.S. Embassy Tokyo Despatch No. 5682 (dated June 23, 1941) transmitting Report No. 1676 on political and economic conditions in Japan during May 1941. The first part (pages 207-237) is the concluding portion of a duplicate copy of the report, reviewing Japanese military operations in China, diplomacy with Indochina and the Netherlands East Indies, internal political developments, economic controls, and comprehensive lists of telegrams and despatches sent during the month. The second part (pages 238-275) begins the complete official copy of Despatch No. 5682 and Report No. 1676, featuring Ambassador Joseph C. Grew's frank exchanges with Foreign Minister Yōsuke Matsuoka over U.S. convoying and the Tripartite Pact, followed by the identical thematic sections and the opening pages of the monthly telegram list.",
 "subfiles": [
